Chat backend (./chatbackend on the server): take every user's name and avatar
from their profile, never from the app.

The server stored whatever the app sent — a user's own x-name / x-avatar
headers, and the peerName / peerAvatar of someone who had never opened chat —
so anyone could appear in pushes and chat lists under any name. Now
auth_user.js and POST /chat/dm/conversations ask
public.chat_profile_card(id) (username, avatar_url) over the existing
chat_blocks_ro connection (oci-backend/sql/chat_profile_card.sql). Cached for
10 minutes; if the lookup fails the stored values stay. Opening a chat also
puts the profile's name back on an older peer row.

Applied on the server 2026-10-31 (backups: <file>.bak-names next to each file).
Apply after chat-blocks.patch:
  cd ~/treepnet/chatbackend && patch -p1 < chat-names-from-profiles.patch
  cd .. && docker compose build chatbackend && docker compose up -d chatbackend

